     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"font-size:14px;clear:both;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Arial,&#39;Liberation Sans&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans&#39;,sans-serif;line-height:17.8048000335693px;background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\">Just asked this over on StackOverflow, so I apologize for cross posting, but I thought I might have more luck with a response here.</p><p style=\"font-size:14px;clear:both;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Arial,&#39;Liberation Sans&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans&#39;,sans-serif;line-height:17.8048000335693px;background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\">I am devoping a shiny application that connects to a database with several tables that each one of these has several thousands rows and is very few cases a few hundrends of thousands of rows (not more than 500,000 rows). The plan is to create an application that will graphicly present either via charts (using ggplot2 and googleVis) or via tables.</p><p style=\"font-size:14px;clear:both;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Arial,&#39;Liberation Sans&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans&#39;,sans-serif;line-height:17.8048000335693px;background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\">As certain piece of data will be used ceveral times in various charts or tables my question is the following: Would it be more efficient (from an application&#39;s performance perspective) to query some of the most frequently used datasets when the application starts (in global.r) or query the database every time I want to make a plot?</p><p style=\"font-size:14px;clear:both;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Arial,&#39;Liberation Sans&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans&#39;,sans-serif;line-height:17.8048000335693px;background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\">Here are a few cases that describe more specifically the above question:</p><ul style=\"margin:0px 0px 1em 30px;padding:0px;border:0px;font-size:14px;vertical-align:baseline;list-style-position:initial;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Arial,&#39;Liberation Sans&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans&#39;,sans-serif;line-height:17.8048000335693px;background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><li style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;font-size:14px;vertical-align:baseline;background:transparent\">Case1<ul style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 30px;padding:0px;border:0px;font-size:14px;vertical-align:baseline;list-style:disc;background:transparent\"><li style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;font-size:14px;vertical-align:baseline;background:transparent\">Query table ABC once in global R and create dataframe &quot;df&quot;</li><li style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;font-size:14px;vertical-align:baseline;background:transparent\">Create a reactive dataset using ABC: &quot;dataformychart&quot;.</li><li style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;font-size:14px;vertical-align:baseline;background:transparent\">Plot output$mychartusing dataformychart()</li></ul></li><li style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;font-size:14px;vertical-align:baseline;background:transparent\">Case 1b<ul style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 30px;padding:0px;border:0px;font-size:14px;vertical-align:baseline;list-style:disc;background:transparent\"><li style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;font-size:14px;vertical-align:baseline;background:transparent\">query table ABC once in global R and create dataframe &quot;df&quot;</li><li style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;font-size:14px;vertical-align:baseline;background:transparent\">plot output$mychart using only required data by slicing &quot;df&quot; within output$mychart</li></ul></li><li style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;font-size:14px;vertical-align:baseline;background:transparent\">Case 2</li><ul style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 30px;padding:0px;border:0px;font-size:14px;vertical-align:baseline;list-style:disc;background:transparent\"><li style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;font-size:14px;vertical-align:baseline;background:transparent\">create a reactive dataset named &quot;dataformychart&quot; and within this query the database</li><li style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;font-size:14px;vertical-align:baseline;background:transparent\">plot output$mychart using dataformychart()</li></ul></ul><div><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Arial, Liberation Sans, DejaVu Sans, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"><span style=\"line-height:17px\"><br></span></font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Arial, Liberation Sans, DejaVu Sans, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"><span style=\"line-height:17px\">Christos</span></font></div></div>"
